** Arbitrary order Exchange-Correlation library **

By Ulf Ekstrom and Radovan Bast 2009. Based on the dft
implementation of Dirac, which was largly written by
Pawel Salek for the Dalton program.

The main interface is in xc_fun.h (or xc_funf.h for Fortran bindings).

NOTES: Due to the way C++ deals with templates all the functionals are
defined in xxx_fun.h files. These are included and instantiated from
xc_fun.cpp, which is the only object file generated by the library.


Compiling the Fortran test program: One way of compiling (with
GCC/GFortran) and linking example.f90 is to do

g++ -c xc_fun.cpp
gfortran -cpp example.f90 xc_fun.o -lstdc++

